# Godfrey dialog state

When changing Godfrey body animation, idle selection, listening/speaking holds, or presence flow, respect **in-dialog vs out-of-dialog**.

## Meaning

- **Out of dialog:** game start (SeaIdle), or after a farewell AS has started / finished (returning to sea).
- **In dialog:** from engage until farewell begins. A new visitor’s first turn is **webcam presence** (arrival card then Welcome / R17), not the microphone. Visitor speech engages only after that Welcome, or if the webcam is off.

API: `UGodfreyPerformanceStateComponent::IsInDialog()` (Engaging + Conversing).

Living tracker: `Docs/GodfreyBehaviourRules.md` (R7, R8, R9, R13, R14, R15, R17, R20, R23).

## Animation rules

- **In dialog:** after an optional first Greeting* hold (R15), attentive listening-pool idles only (`ListeningAttentive` / `Curious` / `Concerned` / `Nodding`). Never play looking-out-to-sea idles (`IdleLookingToSea_*`, SeaIdle exhibition hold) as the conversation hold.
- **First dialog hold (R15):** SeaIdle → dialog once uses `DialogGreetingPool` (`GreetingNod` / `SmallSmile` / `HaveASeat` / `Welcome`); then R9 listening deck.
- **In-dialog idle sequencing (R9):** play pool AS as one-shots in a shuffled non-repeating deck; blend AS→AS (do not section-loop one clip).
- **Speaking body (R14):** while speaking, shuffled one-shot deck from `SpeakingIdlePool` (`Describing*`, `SpeakingDescribe*`, `SpeakingExplainDanger`, calm/emphasis) — never section-loop `CalmExplanation` alone. Conversation AS overlay **UpperBody** (spine_01+) over a planted `IdleStanding` DefaultSlot hold so blends cannot skate the whole figure (R20).
- **Speak→listen (R16):** after audio/lipsync ends, keep speaking body ~1s, then long soft blend into Listening*.
- **Out of dialog (R13):** SeaIdle exhibition hold uses a shuffled calm-idle deck (`IdleLookingToSea_*`, standing/weight-shift/rocking, hands behind back) as soft-blended one-shots. Never section-loop a single SeaIdle AS. Do not use `HandsClasped` (drives hands/sleeves through the jacket; R23).
- **Speaking end:** Speaking body AS must end when audible ACE playback ends (audio-end watchdog from `OnAnimationStarted`), not only when HTTP `FinishStream` completes.
- **Idle re-engagement (R10):** after visitor inactivity, engagement prompts are owned by **Unreal**, not Brain timers/web idle nudge. Brain must not speak unsolicited to re-engage. Do not fire a quiet nudge if visitor speech is already detected; abort an in-flight nudge on `speech_started`. After two unanswered engagement prompts, assume they left, return to SeaIdle, then recapture the empty-room webcam baseline after 2s (waiting for the next visitor).
- **Visitor goodbye (R12):** Brain flags `conversationEnd` (and may emit a `[farewell]` cue); Unreal latches it via `RequestConversationEnd` and stays **in dialog** until the goodbye reply has finished speaking, then runs `BeginFarewell` from `NotifyUtteranceEnded`. Never start the farewell straight from the cue.
